      },
      {
        "Id": "rId4",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image55.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "notes": "‹#›"
  },
  {
    "slide": 23,
    "text": "Mitosis\nAfter DNA replication (interphase), cells go through four stages of mitosis before cytokinesis can occur:\nPMAT! \n(Your dog peed on the mat..)",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "1e517574ee7faaae3d25ac3115f0e21847915e014711b420d6b87269a2583a55",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/slideLayout",
        "Target": "../slideLayouts/slideLayout2.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId2",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/notesSlide",
        "Target": "../notesSlides/notesSlide23.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId3",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image23.png"
      }
    ],
    "notes": ""
  },
  {
    "slide": 24,
    "text": "Key events:\nChromatin condenses to form chromosomes\nNuclear membrane breaks down\nCentrioles move to opposite poles of the cell and spindle fibres begin to form (spindle fibres are required to eventually pull the duplicated chromosomes apart)\nAt this stage, each pair of homologous chromosomes has already been duplicated, so the cell contains twice as much DNA than normal\n.\n1. PROPHASE\nNOTE: These examples only show 4 \nchromosomes (2n=4), but remember that a actual human cell would be showing 46 chromosomes (2n=46)",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "f03b416a4c9a579157600c6b705f65e0348f40c73d4e88f1efeb8b91234967f0",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/slideLayout",
        "Target": "../slideLayouts/slideLayout2.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId2",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/notesSlide",
        "Target": "../notesSlides/notesSlide24.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId3",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image24.png"
      }
    ],
    "notes": ""
  },
  {
    "slide": 25,
    "text": "2. METAPHASE \nKey events:\nSpindle fibres attach to the centromere of each chromosome, guiding them to the equator (middle line) of the cell\nDuplicated chromosomes line up in \nsingle file\n, forming the “metaphase plate”\nM for middle!",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "38a09254bec05fd33abee86728b326eb6585086dd45d85378c3d79bc12a87dc5",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/slideLayout",
        "Target": "../slideLayouts/slideLayout2.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId2",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/notesSlide",
        "Target": "../notesSlides/notesSlide25.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId3",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image32.png"
      }
    ],
    "notes": ""
  },
  {
    "slide": 26,
    "text": "3. ANAPHASE\nKey events:\nSpindle fibres shorten and \nsister chromatids\n \nare pulled apart\n from one another; centromeres split\nTwo opposing poles are formed, each with a complete diploid set of DNA",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "7d24daf31bb3280c801e98326688377c586e258910e8d6861e869dfca7a37eda",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/slideLayout",
        "Target": "../slideLayouts/slideLayout3.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId2",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/notesSlide",
        "Target": "../notesSlides/notesSlide26.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId3",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image30.png"
      }
    ],
    "notes": ""
  },
  {
    "slide": 27,
    "text": "3. ANAPHASE",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "98eebd06bc0cadd530b0b581c6d8ba22e5ec7b59bc5e70a8ee3cc146caf104b2",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/slideLayout",
        "Target": "../slideLayouts/slideLayout3.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId2",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/notesSlide",
        "Target": "../notesSlides/notesSlide27.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId3",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image36.png"
      }
    ],
    "notes": "‹#›"
  },
  {
    "slide": 28,
    "text": "4. TELOPHASE\nKey events:\nChromosomes reach opposite poles of the cell\nSpindle fibres break down\nChromosomes begin to unwind into chromatin\nNuclear membrane forms around each new set of genetic info. ",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "b83d791aedb1465a89c2277732a5b7bfb832629ab896d5c107ca7d3074902d3e",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/slideLayout",
        "Target": "../slideLayouts/slideLayout3.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId2",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/notesSlide",
        "Target": "../notesSlides/notesSlide28.xml"
      },
      {
        "Id": "rId3",
        "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
        "Target": "../media/image43.png"
      }
    ],
    "notes": ""
  },
  {
    "slide": 29,
    "text": "Cytokinesis\nCytoplasm, \ncontaining organelles,\n splits to form two identical daughter cells with the same genetic content as the original parent cell\nDaughter cells are now in G1 of interphase",
    "raw_slide_sha256": "0f238a79c64b6634afbd9d88ea27d5e73d28c90a78eb63d88057076b0cab63b1",
    "relations": [
      {
        "Id": "rId1",
